<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-March 14.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-March 14.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Thursday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name			P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	 360.37   7.82</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	   281.25   1.35</p>
<p> 3   Mt Edon Gold	   246.15   2.24</p>
<p> 4   Ranger Minerals	200.96   4.20</p>
<p> 5   Perilya Mines	  200.00   0.86</p>
<p> 6   Westpac Prop Tr	110.62   1.77</p>
<p> 7   St.Barbara Mine	108.45   0.77</p>
<p> 8   Consol Paper	    83.82   2.85</p>
<p> 9   Devex		     81.11   0.37</p>
<p>10   Tap Oil		   67.05   1.18</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Climax Mining	    2.08   1.03</p>
<p> 2   Jardine Fm China	 4.50   0.67</p>
<p> 3   Consol Rutile	    4.64   1.04</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		    5.89   5.48</p>
<p> 5   OLS Asia Hldgs	   6.97   0.83</p>
<p> 6   Aust Gold Rsc	    7.23   1.32</p>
<p> 7   Adel Bton Cement	 7.51   1.80</p>
<p> 8   BT Aust Eq Mgmt	  7.52   0.76</p>
<p> 9   Premier Inv		7.61   1.35</p>
<p>10   Templeton Global	 7.77   1.43</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
